Let's check how `.menu-item.folder-tile` can have a subtle 3D parallax tilt effect on mouse move.
In `Controller` or `View`, we can add a method or event binder `bindFolderTileParallax()` that listens to `mousemove` on `.menu-item.folder-tile` elements:
```javascript
  bindFolderTileParallax() {
    document.querySelectorAll('.menu-item.folder-tile').forEach((tile) => {
      tile.addEventListener('mousemove', (e) => {
        const rect = tile.getBoundingClientRect();
        const x = e.clientX - rect.left;
        const y = e.clientY - rect.top;
        const xc = rect.width / 2;
        const yc = rect.height / 2;
        const dx = (x - xc) / xc; // -1 to 1
        const dy = (y - yc) / yc; // -1 to 1
        tile.style.transform = `perspective(600px) rotateY(${dx * 8}deg) rotateX(${dy * -8}deg) scale(1.02)`;
      });
      tile.addEventListener('mouseleave', () => {
        tile.style.transform = 'perspective(600px) rotateY(0deg) rotateX(0deg) scale(1)';
      });
    });
  }
```
And call `this.bindFolderTileParallax()` in `Controller.init()`.
